Spawn: a goal list run in a fork of this parsed image, the way a served request runs,
without the socket. The child is not a sub-make: no re-parse, no new MAKELEVEL, one job
slot and no jobserver, and it leaves through die with make's status. amk_wait_child
collects a spawned child by pid or any of them, blocking or not. make's own reap_children
waits on any pid, so a spawned child it collects first is parked by amk_reap_foreign and
handed over on the next wait; a pid it never spawned stays ignored as before. Lua exposes
the api as amk.spawn, amk.wait and amk.kill.

--- a/src/amk.h
